Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of the `bench_running` variable, which was previously defined as a non-global variable leading to issues when formats called `sig_timer_emu_tick()` during benchmarking on systems with `OS_TIMER=0`. This resulted in unintended behavior as the timer emulation function was being called even when benchmarking was not running, which could disrupt the process and lead to errors. The solution involved making `bench_running` a global variable to ensure proper access and control of the benchmarking state across different components of the software.
